{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":20780,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02036ae7fbf10a7af9b25303b03727fa","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Media components have image fills and vector children I can recolor. Workspace is empty. Now build:\n\nPlan:\n1. In Workspace (page 5:2), create:\n   - Local components: copied instances of media components detached? No — create new components by cloning the media components into workspace page. Actually components can live on any page. I'll clone each media component into the Workspace page (clone preserves component type), place them in a \"Components\" area frame.\n   - Build Button variants (default given, hover) — clone the Button component too.\n   - Then build 01_Home frame 1440 wide with sections: Header, Hero, Tech stack (\"EXPERIENCE WITH\"), Projects, Experience, Contact (footer).\n   \nNote: The Button given is white bg with dark text. On a dark page, a white pill button works well as primary CTA (\"Get In Touch\"). \"Download CV\" could be a ghost/outline button variant.\n\nLayout plan (1440 wide, margins ~96px, content 1248):\n- Header: Logo_ABM left, nav right (Home/Projects/Experience/Contact), Home current (orange accent underline or pill). Sticky-ish, dark bg.\n- Hero: left text (title \"I do code and make content about it!\", paragraph, buttons Get In Touch + Download CV), right avatar photo in styled frame with gradient ring.\n- Tech: \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" label, row of 5 logos recolored to light.\n- Projects: heading \"Projects\", two cards side by side: photo, \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\", title HTML TUTORIAL / CSS TUTORIAL, arrow icon.\n- Experience: heading, 3 entries each with initials mark (S/MS/OC), role at company, dates, description.\n- Contact footer: \"Contact\", the seasoned... paragraph, email with mail icon, social icons.\n\nDesign system:\n- bg: #0B0C10 (near black), surface #15161C, surface-2 #1C1E26, border #262832\n- text primary #F5F6F8, secondary #A6AAB5, muted #7C8190\n- accents #D5491D (orange), #1373D1 (blue)\n- Poppins type scale: hero 48 semi, section 32/36, body 16, small 14.\n\nComponents to create in workspace: Button (default + hover variant set?), Nav item, Tech logo chip, Project card, Experience entry, Company mark, Social button. Keep reasonable given tool limits. Build in manageable sections.\n\nLet me start: clone media components into workspace, create local design tokens, build Header + Hero first.\n\nCoordinates: I'll place components area to the left/right of the main frame. Main frame 01_Home at x=0,y=0; components area frame at x=-1600 maybe, or place components off to the right at x=2200.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create local components in workspace page by cloning: Logo_ABM, Photo_Avatar, Photo_Project_HTML, Photo_Project_CSS, Logo_JS, Logo_Nextjs, Logo_HTML5, Logo_CSS3, Logo_React, Logo_Instagram, Logo_X, Logo_YouTube, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right, Icon_Mail, Button.\n2. Recolor logo vector children to light (#F5F6F8 or accent) — brief says \"recolor them for the dark page\".\n3. Build main frame sections.\n\nCareful: cloning a COMPONENT node into another page works. Instances created with createInstance().\n\nLet me do step 1 + create base components in one call, then build the page in several calls.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"f5233cbc-9e1f-48df-bc06-9536ca1c0a0a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:57:13.522Z","thinking_duration_ms":17937}
