{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":21404,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae7fc120a7aa4bba407e421b8dd","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Media components cloned. Now let me create local variables for colors and set up components. Let me first define the design system:\n\nColors:\n- Page background: #0E0E11 (near-black)\n- Surface: #16161B\n- Surface hover / card border: #232329\n- Text primary: #F4F4F5\n- Text secondary: #A8A8B0 (muted)\n- Text tertiary: #6E6E78\n- Accent orange: #D5491D\n- Accent blue: #1373D1\n\nNow build the main components in the workspace. I'll organize a \"Components\" area to the right of the frame.\n\nPlan:\n1. Create Button variants? The given Button is 196x58 white pill with Poppins SemiBold 16 text #161513-ish. For \"Get In Touch\" primary CTA, I'll use the Button component instance with text override. For \"Download CV\" secondary — create a variant \"ghost/outline\" style button.\n\nBetter approach: create a new component \"Button/Primary\" using the given style (white bg, dark text), and \"Button/Secondary\" (transparent bg, 1px border, white text). Both as variants in a component set \"Button\". But the given Button is already a component; I can create a variant set by combining. Simpler: keep given Button component (renamed maybe), and create \"Button / Secondary\" component.\n\nActually for cleanliness, I'll create a component set:\n- \"Button\" with variants: Type=Primary (white fill, dark text), Type=Secondary (outline, light text), State=Hover variants? Variants for hover: Primary/Hover (slightly orange?), Secondary/Hover.\n\nI'll keep it simpler:\n- Component \"Button/Primary\" (white bg pill)\n- Component \"Button/Secondary\" (outline pill)\n- Component \"Button/Primary/Hover\" (accent orange bg, white text)\n- Component \"Button/Secondary/Hover\" (border accent, accent text)\n\nActually Figma variant sets would be more \"reusable\". Let me create a variant set \"Button\" with properties Type (Primary/Secondary) and State (Default/Hover). 4 variants. The default Primary/Default will match the given button style. The original given Button component can be the base for Primary/Default.\n\nHmm, combining into variant sets via API is doable: create components then use figma.combineAsVariants. Let me do:\n\n1. Create 4 button components (build each with autolayout: pill radius 100, padding 16x32, text).\n   - Actually given Button has fixed 196x58 with padding 0 and center align. I'll build new ones with padding: horizontal 28, vertical 16, hug contents.\n\n2. combineAsVariants → \"Button\" with Type & State props.\n\nThen build other components:\n- \"Nav / Item\" with variants State=Default/Current/Hover (text 15px Poppins Medium; current has accent underline or accent color; hover lighter).\n- \"Header\" component: logo left, nav right. 1440 wide? Header inside the page frame — I'll make it a component \"Header\" with autolayout, width 1312 (content width), logo left, nav group right.\n- \"Tech / Logo\" — wrapper? The tech logos are components themselves; I'll just instance them in a row \"TechStack\" inside the page. Maybe create component \"Tech / Item\" = logo instance (recolored white?) The media says tech logos supplied in neutral #1A1A1F, recolor for dark page. They're vectors; instance fills can be overridden? For a vector inside a component instance, we can override fills via instance children? Vector fill override within instance is allowed (instances allow overriding fills of child layers). Yes, you can set fills on instance's vector children.\n- \"Project / Card\": photo, overlay \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\", title row with title text + arrow icon. Variants? State Default/Hover maybe (hover: image scale or border accent). I'll make variants Type=HTML/CSS? No — same structure, different content; instances with overrides. Make one component \"Project / Card\" with default & hover variants.\n- \"Experience / Entry\": initials mark (draw as circle/rounded square with initials), role + company, dates, description.\n- \"Company / Mark\": variants S, MS, OC.\n- \"Contact / Footer\": heading \"Contact\", description, email with mail icon, social logos row.\n- \"Avatar / Hero\": avatar photo with decorative ring/gradient.\n\nNow page layout (1440 wide, dark):\n- Header: fixed top, content 1312 centered: Logo_ABM (white signature, size maybe 100x49 scaled), nav: Home (current), Projects, Experience, Contact.\n- Hero: left text: \"I do code and make content about it!\" (H1, big), paragraph, buttons Get In Touch (primary) + Download CV (secondary). Right: avatar photo in circle with orange/blue gradient ring.\n- Tech stack: \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" small caps label, row of 5 tech logos (recolored light).\n- Projects: heading \"Projects\", two cards side by side (each ~640 wide): photo top (390x235 scaled to fill 640x386?), below: \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\" small caps accent + title \"HTML TUTORIAL\" + arrow icon.\n- Experience: heading \"Experience\", 3 entries stacked. Each: mark circle left, content right: role+company bold, dates muted, description.\n- Contact footer: \"Contact\" heading, description, email button-ish row with mail icon \"abm@example.com\", social icons (Instagram, X, YouTube). Footer bottom maybe divider + small copyright? Not required; keep minimal but nice.\n\nLet me also create color variables collection \"ABM\" with tokens: bg/page, bg/surface, border, text/primary, text/secondary, text/muted, accent/orange, accent/blue. And maybe use them in fills via boundVariables? Simpler: create paint styles. Variables are nicer. I'll create variables and bind where convenient (may be time-consuming; I'll bind on main fills).\n\nGiven effort constraints, I'll use variables for core colors and bind them in the built components. Actually binding via API: fill = figma.variables.setBoundVariableForPaint(paint, 'color', variable). Doable. I'll do it for page bg and key surfaces. To keep manageable, I'll bind in a helper function whenever creating solids.\n\nLet me write a big build script in stages:\n\nStage 1: variables + text styles maybe skip text styles; just variables.\nStage 2: Button variants set + Nav item variants + Header component.\nStage 3: Company mark variants + Experience entry + Project card + Footer/contact bits + Avatar block (as components).\nStage 4: Assemble 01_Home frame with instances, all text, sections.\nStage 5: Screenshot, verify, fix.\n\nLayout plan for 01_Home (1440 wide, autolayout vertical):\n- Header section (height ~96): content row padding 64/64? Content width 1312 (64px margins as in brief pages).\n- Hero: padding 64 sides, row, gap 80: left column (badge? no), H1 56px, body 16px, buttons row; right avatar 320 with gradient ring.\n- Tech: centered column: label \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" 13px letterspaced muted, row of logos gap 56.\n- Projects: label + H2 \"Projects\"? Brief must-include says Projects section with title \"Projects\". Two cards 644 each gap 24 (like brief frame cards).\n- Experience: H2 \"Experience\", entries.\n- Contact: centered: H2 \"Contact\", description max 640, email row, socials.\n- Footer bottom bar: small text? Optional — maybe \"© 2026 ABM\" not required... skip to avoid non-fixed copy? \"Copy and data must match Fixed data exactly\" — adding a copyright line is extra copy; safer to avoid any extra text beyond required. I'll avoid decorative text. Small labels like \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" are required. OK.\n\nNav current state: \"Home\" with orange accent underline and white text; others muted.\n\nHover states: defined as variants in components (documented in the components area). Since single frame, hover variants are shown in component library area.\n\nLet me start coding. I'll write helper functions in each script since state doesn't persist between calls... Actually the Figma plugin API code runs fresh each time; helpers must be redefined. I'll keep scripts self-contained.\n\nStage 1: create variables.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"c0d5ecb5-7770-4c2d-ba38-ea25b7045d78","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:58:12.748Z","thinking_duration_ms":43533}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":21404,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae7fc120a7aa4bba407e421b8dd","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Media assets cloned to workspace. Now I'll set up the design system: color variables, then build components (Button variants, Nav items, Header, Company marks, Experience entry, Project card)."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"19c18cec-2224-464d-8e49-7d6124eb8bea","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:58:13.700Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":21404,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02206ae7fc120a7aa4bba407e421b8dd","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_12_7c43194a","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\n// Stage 1: color variables\nconst coll = figma.variables.createVariableCollection('ABM Tokens');\nconst modeId = coll.modes[0].modeId;\nfunction mkVar(name, hex) {\n  const v = figma.variables.createVariable(name, coll, 'COLOR');\n  const r = parseInt(hex.slice(1,3),16)/255, g = parseInt(hex.slice(3,5),16)/255, b = parseInt(hex.slice(5,7),16)/255;\n  v.setValueForMode(modeId, {r,g,b});\n  return v.id;\n}\nconst vars = {\n  page: mkVar('bg/page', '#0C0C10'),\n  surface: mkVar('bg/surface', '#15151B'),\n  surface2: mkVar('bg/surface-raised', '#1C1C24'),\n  border: mkVar('border/subtle', '#2A2A33'),\n  textPrimary: mkVar('text/primary', '#F5F5F7'),\n  textSecondary: mkVar('text/secondary', '#A9A9B4'),\n  textMuted: mkVar('text/muted', '#6F6F7B'),\n  orange: mkVar('accent/orange', '#D5491D'),\n  blue: mkVar('accent/blue', '#1373D1'),\n  onOrange: mkVar('accent/on-orange', '#FFFFFF'),\n};\nreturn vars;\n","description":"Create color variable tokens","fileKey":"7Jay53n2t4eIv7n3PmNRTh"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"89355d13-cad6-415c-a94c-21ee1326290c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:58:18.783Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_12_7c43194a","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_12_7c43194a","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"page\":\"VariableID:8:3\",\"surface\":\"VariableID:8:4\",\"surface2\":\"VariableID:8:5\",\"border\":\"VariableID:8:6\",\"textPrimary\":\"VariableID:8:7\",\"textSecondary\":\"VariableID:8:8\",\"textMuted\":\"VariableID:8:9\",\"orange\":\"VariableID:8:10\",\"blue\":\"VariableID:8:11\",\"onOrange\":\"VariableID:8:12\"}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"4a455bc7-8ee0-4b40-a0e9-49c0e45ff956","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:58:23.218Z","tool_use_result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"page\":\"VariableID:8:3\",\"surface\":\"VariableID:8:4\",\"surface2\":\"VariableID:8:5\",\"border\":\"VariableID:8:6\",\"textPrimary\":\"VariableID:8:7\",\"textSecondary\":\"VariableID:8:8\",\"textMuted\":\"VariableID:8:9\",\"orange\":\"VariableID:8:10\",\"blue\":\"VariableID:8:11\",\"onOrange\":\"VariableID:8:12\"}"}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"b695b2eb-c40b-454d-80e8-4590eff09af7"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_12_7c43194a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":22028,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"081b6ae7fc4f0a7ad4bf4680d9ae34e2","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_13_b1d815d6","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\n// Stage 2: load fonts + recolor media components to light\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Poppins', style:'Regular'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Poppins', style:'Medium'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Poppins', style:'Semi Bold'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Poppins', style:'Bold'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Poppins', style:'Light'});\n\nconst LIGHT = {r:0.93, g:0.93, b:0.95}; // ~#EEEEF2\nconst ACCENT = {r:0.835, g:0.286, b:0.114}; // #D5491D\n\nasync function recolor(id, color, skip) {\n  const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  const vectors = comp.findAll(n => n.type === 'VECTOR' || n.type === 'BOOLEAN_OPERATION');\n  for (const v of vectors) {\n    if (skip && skip(v)) continue;\n    v.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color}];\n  }\n  return {name: comp.name, count: vectors.length};\n}\nconst results = [];\nfor (const id of ['7:8','7:10','7:14','7:16','7:18','7:20','7:22','7:24','7:26','7:4']) {\n  results.push(await recolor(id, LIGHT));\n}\n// JavaScript logo: has a yellow bg square + JS letters; make square accent orange and letters light\nconst js = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:12');\nconst jsVecs = js.findAll(n => n.type === 'VECTOR' || n.type === 'BOOLEAN_OPERATION');\nconst jsInfo = jsVecs.map(v => ({name: v.name, w: v.width, h: v.height}));\nfor (const v of jsVecs) {\n  // background square is the largest\n  if (v.width > 30) v.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color: ACCENT}];\n  else v.fills = [{type:'SOLID', color: {r:1,g:1,b:1}}];\n}\nreturn {results, jsInfo};\n","description":"Load Poppins fonts and recolor logo components to light on dark","fileKey":"7Jay53n2t4eIv7n3PmNRTh"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"1e81e0cd-9e88-41f4-9bc9-2e440a79d122","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:58:56.602Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_13_b1d815d6","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
