{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":60426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041e6ae7ffff0a7a587e12ecdd2aa48e","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the design. Problems visible:\n\n1. **Project cards render as tiny photos** — cards show only a sliver of the photo at top; the card body (kicker + title) is missing/clipped. The Project Card instance in the row seems to show only ~80px tall photo region. Actually looking at it, cards appear as wide rectangles showing a cropped photo strip with no body text. The card height is 460, photo 366 + body 94. In screenshot, cards look ~90px tall. Something wrong — the photo wrap is `layoutAlign: STRETCH` with fixed 360 height, but since the card is vertical auto-layout... the body frame's layoutGrow=1, and photo wrap layoutAlign=STRETCH applies to cross-axis (width) in vertical layout — but its height is FIXED 360. Hmm, but the render shows cards much shorter than 460. Also the Experience entries show placeholder text \"Description text\" — wait, they show \"Lead Software Engineer at Searchlight\" ×3 and \"Description text\"! The character overrides got LOST — because of `entry.resetOverrides?.()` which I called in the previous step! resetOverrides reset all text overrides back to the component default. Damn. So all 3 entries now show the component's default text.\n\nWait — but the marks still show \"S\" for all three... yes, all reset.\n\n2. Project cards: heights were 460 in metadata earlier. But screenshot shows them ~90 tall. Let me look again: The Projects section shows two rounded rectangles with photo content at top, and there's clearly a small orange dot in the left card. The card appears to be rendering photo-only at a smaller scale? Actually the cards look about 470px wide × 90 tall in the 1105-wide display → original ~610 × 117. So cards are rendering at 608×~117?? The body is missing and photo is cropped. Maybe the photoWrap resize... no. Actually, earlier `cards` reported `h: 460` for both. But screenshot shows otherwise. Unless the screenshot was taken before... no, order was fine.\n\nHmm wait, look closer: the left card shows a dark photo with orange lamps — that's the HTML project image; the right shows CSS image. Both are cropped to a horizontal strip at the top of the card region, and the rest (title area) seems to be cut off / not visible. Perhaps the body frame (kicker, title) has zero height and the photo is 360 tall but the card renders... no.\n\nActually — I bet the issue is the same counterAxisSizingMode trap inside the Project Card component: the card is VERTICAL layout; counter axis is horizontal. The \"Photo\" frame was resized to 608×360 while being a direct child with layoutAlign STRETCH (cross-axis = width stretch — good), its primary (vertical) sizing FIXED 360. Body: layoutAlign STRETCH + layoutGrow 1 — with primary sizing... I set body.layoutGrow = 1 after appendChild. Should be fine.\n\nBut the card's height is FIXED 460 — I set primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED and resize(608,460). The instances in the row should render 460 tall. But screenshot shows short cards. UNLESS: the cardsRow children — earlier I queried cards w/h = 608×460. And screenshot shows ~117 tall. Contradiction... unless the vertical scale of screenshot differs — no, sections above measure correctly.\n\nHmm, wait — looking again at the image: Projects section — I see \"Projects\" heading, then two rounded-corner photo strips. The photo strips look like ~90px tall each in the scaled-down image (1105 wide). 90×1.3 = 117. The body area with kicker+title would add ~94. Photo 360. Total should be ~460×(1/1.3) = 354px in display. The displayed strips are much shorter.\n\nOH WAIT. I see it — in the screenshot, the cards are displayed but the PHOTO fills only a strip. Maybe the photo instance itself got clipped and the body exists but is invisible... no, body would show text.\n\nAlternatively the card instances collapsed because when I did swapComponent on the photo, the new instance size differed (Photo_Project_CSS is 390×235 vs HTML 390×235 — same). Hmm.\n\nLet me just inspect the live values again rather than speculate.\n\n3. The experience entries show wrong text (reset issue) — need to re-apply overrides and NOT call resetOverrides.\n\n4. Footer: looks good! Contact title, description, email pill, social row, bottom bar all render. Though bottom bar copyright is at right, logo at left — fine.\n\n5. Tech logos: all render white — JS logo shows orange square with white JS — looks good. But they're small; spacing fine.\n\n6. Hero looks great.\n\n7. The \"Get In Touch\" button in header looks good. Nav current \"Home\" has orange dot — visible.\n\n8. Projects section: cards need fixing. Let me inspect.\n\nAlso note: Experience \"Description text\" placeholders — need re-applying real text.\n\nPlan:\n- Inspect card instances in home: their actual height & children.\n- Fix: possibly re-create card instances.\n- Re-apply experience overrides.\n- Re-screenshot.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"1e385f4b-b00d-4955-b10e-1d352d8b78f0","timestamp":"2026-11-02T03:14:44.825Z","thinking_duration_ms":26385}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":60426,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041e6ae7ffff0a7a587e12ecdd2aa48e","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_54_703ad85e","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst home = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('16:2');\nconst projSec = home.findOne(n => n.name === 'Section / Projects');\nconst cardsRow = projSec.findOne(n => n.name === 'Cards row');\nconst out = [];\nfor (const card of cardsRow.children) {\n  out.push({\n    w: Math.round(card.width), h: Math.round(card.height),\n    sizing: [card.primaryAxisSizingMode, card.counterAxisSizingMode],\n    layoutAlign: card.layoutAlign,\n    children: card.children.map(c => ({name: c.name, w: Math.round(c.width), h: Math.round(c.height), visible: c.visible})),\n  });\n}\nreturn out;\n","description":"Inspect project card instances actual sizes","fileKey":"7Jay53n2t4eIv7n3PmNRTh"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"6628cee2-b368-4200-91ed-e025f2bac67f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T03:14:47.561Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_54_703ad85e","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
