{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":101264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02106ae806d20a7af2f09f23cf76e8e4","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The workspace overview shows the library — but the screenshot only shows the library area (01_Home is at x=0, library at x=1700; the page screenshot seems to only cover x≥1700 region? Actually the screenshot shows the library only. The page screenshot probably crops to content bounding box; width 1500 suggests it captured only the library area... odd, maybe get_screenshot of a page captures the viewport of content. Whatever — individual screenshots verify content.\n\nLibrary observations:\n1. Media stage: components overflow the stage frame (CSS Magic image hangs outside the right edge, JS logo too). Media stage width 700 is too small — the resize logic had a bug (`mx + n.width + pad > 1440 - 0` condition wrong). Also caption text is white on white outside frame? Captions are below stage, on page bg — they're greyish, fine.\n2. Buttons & Nav stage: nav variants show \"Home Home Home\" — all three variants say \"Home\" (that's by design since the component text is 'Home'; variant labels show default/hover/current states though visually similar). The current variant underline seems missing in preview? There's a faint dot maybe. Minor.\n3. Sections & Cards: header shows Get In Touch button ✓, tech row ✓, cards ✓, experience entry ✓, social buttons row ✓, contact section ✓. All on dark stage ✓.\n\nFix: widen media stage so all media fits; check my resize math — width ended at 700 because `Math.max(mx - gap + pad, 700)`. mx accumulates across rows; final mx after last row... The row wrap condition was buggy: `if (mx + n.width + pad > 1440 && mx > pad)` — wrapping at 1440 but the stage then resized to max(mx...) which could be large. Result 700 means rows wrapped and final mx was small. Actually the row heights: avatar 200 tall, project images ~366 tall at original sizes — the components were cloned at original sizes (Photo_Project_HTML 390x235). Let me just resize media stage to fit contents by computing bounds.\n\nLet me fix by measuring children bounds and resizing the stage to fit, then re-flow rows to a max width of ~1440.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"7d180c57-2b1f-4b0f-b2b5-07003e0aec48","timestamp":"2026-11-02T03:43:52.900Z","thinking_duration_ms":10740}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":101264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02106ae806d20a7af2f09f23cf76e8e4","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_113_7692a10b","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('5:2');\nconst media = page.children.find(c => c.name === 'Library · Media');\nconst pad = 32, gap = 28, maxW = 1420;\nlet mx = pad, my = pad, rowH = 0, widest = 0;\nconst caption = media.children.find(c => c.type === 'TEXT');\nfor (const n of media.children) {\n  if (n === caption) continue;\n  if (mx > pad && mx + n.width > maxW) { mx = pad; my += rowH + gap; rowH = 0; }\n  n.x = mx; n.y = my;\n  mx += n.width + gap;\n  rowH = Math.max(rowH, n.height);\n  widest = Math.max(widest, n.x + n.width);\n}\nmedia.resize(widest + pad, my + rowH + pad);\ncaption.x = pad;\ncaption.y = media.height + 12;\nreturn {mediaW: media.width, mediaH: media.height};\n","description":"Reflow media stage to fit all media components","fileKey":"7Jay53n2t4eIv7n3PmNRTh"}}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcabb8c3-59d8-498d-9399-29c448a10028","uuid":"eaf2f846-eb8d-43bd-bf8d-203181fd7b94","timestamp":"2026-11-02T03:43:56.799Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"mcp__figma__use_figma_113_7692a10b","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
